### Smoke test: codex --help runs without auth

Source: https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/cli/e2e_benches/codex_help.rs

The e2e benchmark spawns `codex --help` and asserts success, confirming the help flag works without authentication

```rust
fn codex_help(bencher: Bencher) {
    let codex = codex_utils_cargo_bin::cargo_bin("codex")
        .expect("codex binary should be available through Bazel runfiles");

    bencher.bench_local(move || {
        let output = Command::new(&codex)
            .arg("--help")
            .output()
            .expect("codex --help should run");
        assert!(output.status.success(), "codex --help should succeed");
    });
}
```

### Quickstart > Installing and running Codex CLI

Source: https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/README.md

Codex CLI can be installed on macOS, Linux, and Windows using standalone installers, package managers like npm and Homebrew, or by downloading pre-built binaries. The standalone installers download from OpenAI's release servers by default and fall back to GitHub Releases if a metadata or asset download is unavailable.

### Configure Environment Variables for HTTP(S) Proxy

Source: https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/network-proxy/README.md

Set these environment variables to direct HTTP, HTTPS, WS, and WSS traffic through the `codex-network-proxy`.

```bash
export HTTP_PROXY="http://127.0.0.1:3128"
export HTTPS_PROXY="http://127.0.0.1:3128"
export WS_PROXY="http://127.0.0.1:3128"
export WSS_PROXY="http://127.0.0.1:3128"
```

