### Audit CLI subcommands: doctor, mcp, plugin, features

Source: https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/cli/src/main.rs

Defines the CLI subcommands for auditing Codex configuration: `codex doctor` (diagnose installation, config, auth, runtime health), `codex mcp list/get` (list/inspect MCP servers), `codex plugin list` (list installed plugins), and `codex features list` (list feature flags with stage and effective state).

```rust
enum Subcommand {
    /// Diagnose local Codex installation, config, auth, and runtime health.
    Doctor(DoctorCommand),

    /// Manage external MCP servers for Codex.
    Mcp(McpCli),

    /// Manage Codex plugins.
    Plugin(PluginCli),

    /// Inspect feature flags.
    Features(FeaturesCli),
}

// MCP subcommands (cli/src/mcp_cmd.rs):
// - list   — list configured servers (with --json)
// - get    — show a single server (with --json)

// Plugin subcommands (cli/src/plugin_cmd.rs):
// - list   — list plugins with --json/--available/--marketplace
// - add/remove — install/uninstall plugins

// Features subcommands:
// - list   — List known features with their stage and effective state
// - enable — Enable a feature in config.toml
// - disable — Disable a feature in config.toml
```

