### Running Codex CLI as API Service with WebSocket

Source: https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/main/codex-rs/app-server/README.md

To convert Codex CLI to an API service, run the app-server binary with websocket transport. This exposes a JSON-RPC 2.0 endpoint that can accept remote connections. The server also provides health check endpoints (GET /readyz and /healthz).

```bash
# Launch Codex app-server as API service listening on websocket
codex app-server --listen ws://0.0.0.0:8080

# Health check endpoints exposed:
# GET /readyz - Returns 200 OK once listener is accepting connections
# GET /healthz - Returns 200 OK when no Origin header is present

# Clients connect via WebSocket and send JSON-RPC 2.0 messages:
# Each message is one JSON-RPC message per websocket text frame
```
